answers.workaround:
It has [previously been proposed](https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/hzen7x/comment/fzio3pw/?utm_source=reddit&utm_medium=web2x&context=3) to manipulate layers temporarily during checks.

An alternative solution would be gathering all objects from the scene tree and adding them to the blacklist. Then, the target objects are erased before calling the function:

```gdscript
func get_all_children(in_node, arr:=[]) -> Array:
	arr.push_back(in_node)
	for child in in_node.get_children():
		arr = get_all_children(child, arr)
	return arr

func intersect_ray_to(position: Vector3) -> Dictionary:
	var exclude_objs := get_all_children(get_tree().root)
	exclude_objs.erase(collision_body)
	return get_world().direct_space_state.intersect_ray(position, global_transform.origin, exclude_objs)
```

Either solution is very harsh on performance.
